{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/960874-how-to-use-sam-height","id":960874,"title":"How to use Sam Height?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-30T21:51:35-07:00","id":960874,"title":"How to use Sam Height?","content":"Im quite interested in using him as a villian in my game (a la Dio Brando) but not as op like he used to be. I know he was a walking parody. But as i read Skinners, i find myself more And more interested to using him in a more &quot;Down to earth&quot; way. To ST his arc And to jump to Skinners. Any advices on his stats And how to use him?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T22:49:53-07:00","id":960896,"title":"","content":"In the purely Werewolf context he was great - a bitter kinfolk who discovered a Wyrm-rite to become Garou and murders Garou to do it, becoming the first Skin-Thief. Great! Go with that!<br /> <br /> Just don't then make him a powerful Ghoul, who also has a magical staff that lets him wield Sphere-magick with infinite Mana! That's where he became a bad joke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-31-2016, 02:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T23:03:10-07:00","id":960901,"title":"","content":"A jilted kinfolk who steals Garou pelts is a perfectly horrifying antagonist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T23:36:33-07:00","id":960913,"title":"","content":"And if needed, and the group kills HIM, perhaps someone else takes on the role of &quot;Sam Height&quot;..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T00:24:48-07:00","id":960931,"title":"","content":"Sammy wasn't an OP character until he started stealing mage Powers. Without it he is just a clever strong Skin Danser, that is ghouled, so if you really want you can give him one dot of Potence, Celerity and Fortitude, that knew some Sorcery. All these things cost Experience, and his Gift Selection were very limited, compared to a kosher Garou Elder his magical powers would be considerably more limited as he doesn't really have access to anything but the most basic and corrupt gifts. He would definitely stand a chance in hell against Gol-gol Fangs first, or even Maria Cabrah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T01:08:14-07:00","id":960938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/960874-how-to-use-sam-height?p=960931#post960931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sammy wasn't an OP character until he started stealing mage Powers. Without it he is just a clever strong Skin Danser, that is ghouled, so if you really want you can give him one dot of Potence, Celerity and Fortitude, that knew some Sorcery. All these things cost Experience, and his Gift Selection were very limited, compared to a kosher Garou Elder his magical powers would be considerably more limited as he doesn't really have access to anything but the most basic and corrupt gifts. He would definitely stand a chance in hell against Gol-gol Fangs first, or even Maria Cabrah.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It might not have been as overpowered as the Sphere magick, but the ghouling served no strong purpose and just diluted his narrative. If you want to give him the mechanical benefits of low level Potence Celerity and Fortitude, those can always be easily justified as Wyrm Gifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T01:23:46-07:00","id":960942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/960874-how-to-use-sam-height?p=960938#post960938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It might not have been as overpowered as the Sphere magick, but the ghouling served no strong purpose and just diluted his narrative. If you want to give him the mechanical benefits of low level Potence Celerity and Fortitude, those can always be easily justified as Wyrm Gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true but at least it was possible, and if he became a ghoul before becoming a Skin Danser it does kind of make sense, representing him scouring the Earth for any edge he can get.<br /> <br /> <br /> What I don't do is require Ritual 5 knowledge to become a skin danser, that is preposterous, I just have it 1 person needs to know the ritual and uses it on other. And hell it would probably be safe to have it be a Sorcery ritual and a Fera Ritual. Its just weird as hell for requiring every skin Danser to be super Bruce Lee Brainsurgeon level Ritualists...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T01:55:45-07:00","id":960946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/960874-how-to-use-sam-height?p=960942#post960942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I don't do is require Ritual 5 knowledge to become a skin danser, that is preposterous, I just have it 1 person needs to know the ritual and uses it on other. And hell it would probably be safe to have it be a Sorcery ritual and a Fera Ritual. Its just weird as hell for requiring every skin Danser to be super Bruce Lee Brainsurgeon level Ritualists...</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. A rite-master should be able to turn someone else into a Skin-dancer with the necessary pelts. That creates a useful cult/cult-leader dynamic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T04:13:48-07:00","id":960972,"title":"","content":"I agree on this issue, I started a thread <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/827707-how-do-skindancers-achieve-rituals-5\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ieve-rituals-5</a> <br /> <br /> But as for Haight, he works quite well...<br /> <br /> best way to use him is to give him a random &quot;Pet the dog&quot; moment, to show the players hes not EVIL<br /> <br /> in one anthology, it shows him going out to rescue his former fiance's son... who turned out to be Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T04:47:41-07:00","id":960980,"title":"","content":"I always just figured it was a single high-level ritual that Sam just learned rote. He didn't really understand the underlying theory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T08:30:43-07:00","id":961068,"title":"","content":"What would his stats be? And how he would take down on a Garou in crinos form?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T12:29:27-07:00","id":961166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/960874-how-to-use-sam-height?p=961068#post961068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would his stats be? And how he would take down on a Garou in crinos form?</div> </div> </div> </div>High end stats (physical and mental). Overall, it depends on when in his career you're using him. And to the second question: with silver. Most Crinos can't take full auto with Silver rounds even if they're prepared for a fight. And surprising a Garou with a Silver machete is generally a 1 shot kill. Combats with him should be fast and lethal. The only reason he survived as long as he did is because he does his best to avoid fights he can't win. The moment things go south he should cut and run.<br /> He isn't the threat he is because he can challenge and take on all comers. Skinners are boogeymen. They're frightening because they will kill you and desecrate your corpse, and because they can possibly be any disgruntled kinfolk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T12:34:21-07:00","id":961169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/960874-how-to-use-sam-height?p=961166#post961166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> High end stats (physical and mental). Overall, it depends on when in his career you're using him. And to the second question: with silver. Most Crinos can't take full auto with Silver rounds even if they're prepared for a fight. And surprising a Garou with a Silver machete is generally a 1 shot kill. Combats with him should be fast and lethal. The only reason he survived as long as he did is because he does his best to avoid fights he can't win. The moment things go south he should cut and run.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though it shouldn't be nearly as easy as in any given published adventure. WW wanted to keep him around because of a metaplot with Haight, but STs should be under no obligation to pull that shit if he actually gets caught.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T13:04:18-07:00","id":961188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/960874-how-to-use-sam-height?p=961169#post961169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Though it shouldn't be nearly as easy as in any given published adventure. WW wanted to keep him around because of a metaplot with Haight, but STs should be under no obligation to pull that shit if he actually gets caught.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. No NPC should have plot armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T17:44:08-07:00","id":961993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/960874-how-to-use-sam-height?p=960942#post960942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's true but at least it was possible, and if he became a ghoul before becoming a Skin Danser it does kind of make sense, representing him scouring the Earth for any edge he can get.</div> </div> </div> </div>This right here. Imagine his position: You find out that Werewolves exist... not just that, but Vampires, Ghosts, Wizards and the rest all probably exist as well. Now you're sitting there with a gut-wrenching inferiority complex and a hatred of the Garou... so what do you do? Even with silver bullets, it's dangerous to go after them. They travel in packs... they have weird spirit powers... they have a nasty habit of raging back to life in a murderous berserk frenzy... they have totem spirits following them around that might rat you out later.<br /> <br /> No, you need power. Any and every scrap you can get your hands on.<br /> <br /> That means buying out every occult bookstore you can find and trying to weed out the truth from stacks of love-yourself hippie bull excrement and meditating your way to a more fulfilled you.... until you find something that works. Hedgemagic.<br /> <br /> That means grasping every dirty source of power you've heard of. Vampire lackies can take a bullet without dying? They can bend steel bars and punch through cement? Vampire-hunting Ghoul.<br /> <br /> The voice whispers it can give you power in exchange for just.... just letting it in? The next step is probably infernalism (If you like the old 1st edition material... I don't know how much of that lived through to Revised) or possession. Maybe a Psychomachae that can grow in power with every murder. That's all, of course, if he hasn't gotten those skins that Tibetan shaman (Black Spiral Dancer) told him he needed, first....<br /> <br /> As said before, I agree that Haight was a great villain up until the Sphere magick, even if the backstory for the Rite of Sacred Rebirth was a little wobbly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T12:14:54-07:00","id":962434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/960874-how-to-use-sam-height?p=961993#post961993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This right here. Imagine his position: You find out that Werewolves exist... not just that, but Vampires, Ghosts, Wizards and the rest all probably exist as well. Now you're sitting there with a gut-wrenching inferiority complex and a hatred of the Garou... so what do you do? Even with silver bullets, it's dangerous to go after them. They travel in packs... they have weird spirit powers... they have a nasty habit of raging back to life in a murderous berserk frenzy... they have totem spirits following them around that might rat you out later.<br /> <br /> No, you need power. Any and every scrap you can get your hands on.<br /> <br /> That means buying out every occult bookstore you can find and trying to weed out the truth from stacks of love-yourself hippie bull excrement and meditating your way to a more fulfilled you.... until you find something that works. Hedgemagic.<br /> <br /> That means grasping every dirty source of power you've heard of. Vampire lackies can take a bullet without dying? They can bend steel bars and punch through cement? Vampire-hunting Ghoul.<br /> <br /> The voice whispers it can give you power in exchange for just.... just letting it in? The next step is probably infernalism (If you like the old 1st edition material... I don't know how much of that lived through to Revised) or possession. Maybe a Psychomachae that can grow in power with every murder. That's all, of course, if he hasn't gotten those skins that Tibetan shaman (Black Spiral Dancer) told him he needed, first....<br /> <br /> As said before, I agree that Haight was a great villain up until the Sphere magick, even if the backstory for the Rite of Sacred Rebirth was a little wobbly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could seed hedge magic, but Haight, as a Werewolf-specific serial killer, really should keep to Werewolf. It's not like vampires are easy to find, and at some point he'd probably get fed up with waiting and just go back to his original plans to kill Garou and mystically take their stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}